# {{.ProjectName}}

{{.AgentName}} — an agent on the [agent-base](https://github.com/tankdonut/agent-base) container image. All boot
logic (spec validation, config/MCP/plugin reconciliation, content
seeding, cron scheduling) lives in the base image; this repo contributes
content only: a `spec.json`, seed directories, and image-baked
automations.

## Quick start

Install agentctl once (the agent-base operator CLI):

```sh
# release binary (pick your arch; checksums: agentctl-SHA256SUMS)
curl -fsSL -o ~/bin/agentctl \
  https://github.com/tankdonut/agent-base/releases/download/{{.BaseTag}}/agentctl-linux-amd64
# or build from source
go install ./agent-base/cmd/agentctl   # from a clone of tankdonut/agent-base
```

Then:

```sh
agentctl secrets init   # agent/.env + litellm/.env (gateway token, LiteLLM master/client keys)
agentctl secrets edit   # fill in real values (provider keys go in litellm/.env ONLY)
agentctl secrets check  # verify every required var is set (+ master/client key match)
agentctl deploy         # build + start the stack (podman or docker, auto-detected)
agentctl dev up         # dev overlay: bind-mounted seed content, no rebuild
```

`./make.sh <command>` works as a shim for the same commands.

Models: `litellm/config.yaml` routes `litellm/<alias>` model ids (spec's
`model.fallback` / `automations.model`) to upstream providers; provider
API keys live only in `litellm/.env` — the agent container holds nothing
but the proxy key.

Gateway: <http://localhost:{{.GatewayPort}}/healthz> — loopback-only,
token-authenticated when OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN is set.

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| `fleet.yaml` | THE manifest: roster, gateway ports, plane (shared services) — the only authored deployment shape |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/spec.json` | Declarative boot contract (fail-closed loader) |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/Dockerfile` | Thin project image: FROM agent-base + five COPY lines |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/.env` | Agent secrets (gitignored), created from `agent/.env.example` |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/litellm/config.yaml` | Model routing: `litellm/<alias>` → upstream providers |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/litellm/.env` | Proxy + provider secrets (gitignored); NEVER enters the agent container |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/automations/` | Cron jobs, image-baked (never bind-mounted) |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/workspace/`, `agent/skills/`, `knowledge/content/` | Seed content for the data volume |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/compose.yml` | RENDERED from fleet.yaml on every agentctl verb (gitignored) — never hand-edit |
| `agents/{{.AgentKey}}/compose.dev.yml` | Dev overlay (authored; applied on top of the rendered envelope) |
| `make.sh` | Thin shim over agentctl (`exec agentctl "$@"`) |

A single-agent repo is a fleet of one: add `agents/<name>/` directories
and their `fleet.yaml` registry entries to grow it (`agentctl fleet
ls` / `fleet check` operate the roster).

